## Token model (D6, reproduced exactly)

| chain | post-restart instructions | restarts b/c | a (M) | b (M) | c (M) | pre-boundary P (M) | saving b | saving c | price/input a | price/input b |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| A | 4-7 (4) | 2/2 | 40.9 | 21.5 | 20.7 | 8.1 | 47.4% | 49.4% | 0.138 | 0.185 |
| B | 4-7 (4) | 1/1 | 38.4 | 22.2 | 21.4 | 9.4 | 42.1% | 44.2% | 0.136 | 0.168 |
| C | 5-7 (3) | 1/1 | 33.7 | 22.4 | 21.8 | 11.1 | 33.6% | 35.4% | 0.142 | 0.169 |
| D | 4-7 (4) | 2/2 | 45.6 | 23.7 | 22.9 | 10.3 | 48.0% | 49.8% | 0.134 | 0.178 |

Totals: a 158.5M, b 89.8M, c 86.8M; saving b 43.4%, c 45.3%; post-restart instructions per replicate: 15 of 28.
With the summary-request call charged: b 91.1M, c 88.1M (saving b 42.5%, c 44.4%).
Price units (input side B4 rule + output at 5): a 21.7M, b 15.7M, c 15.1M; price saving b 27.7%, c 30.6%.
Variant, 5-minute cache writes at 1.25: a 20.5M, b 14.3M, c 13.7M; price saving b 30.2%, c 33.1%.
Output share of arm a's price: 12.9%.
Input-side price only: a 18.9M (0.119/token), b 12.6M, c 12.2M. Phase 2 (C3): 0.92M/7.5M = 0.123/token.

## Cost of one replicate (4 chains) by design

Shared pre-boundary input P = 39.0M tokens (25% of arm a). High scenario = model x 1.32 (arm a at the phase 2 rate of 7.5M per instruction, same saving).

| design | input tokens, model | input tokens, high | price units, model | price units, high |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 3 arms, independent runs (a+b+c) | 335M | 444M | 52.5M | 69.5M |
| 2 arms, independent runs (a+b) | 248M | 329M | 37.4M | 49.6M |
| 3 arms, forked at the boundary (a + b-branch + c-branch) | 257M | 341M | 39.1M | 51.8M |
| 2 arms, forked at the boundary (a + b-branch) | 209M | 277M | 30.7M | 40.7M |

